config MICRO_OS_FS_EXT2
    bool "ext2, read and written"
    default n
    help
        Read and write an ext2 volume: the superblock, the group
        descriptors, the inode table, the direct and the indirect blocks,
        the directories, the bitmaps of the groups. A file is created,
        written, cut and removed, a directory is made, and the mode and
        the owner change. A record of ext2 keeps a mode, an owner and the
        moments of a change, so stat, statx and ls -l answer with what the
        medium holds.
